# 2 — CUSTODY / PROJECT RESPONSIBILITY REGISTER

**Project attention:** Max Rupplin — MEARVK LLC — 2026

## Purpose

Record the point at which code enters Ubuntu Determinant project custody and the responsibilities that follow.

## Custody means

Project custody means the project accepts responsibility for:

- preserving applicable licenses and notices;
- maintaining source provenance;
- building and testing the code in its declared environment;
- tracking project modifications;
- documenting integration dependencies;
- recording security and architectural concerns;
- maintaining concords with neighboring components.

## Custody does not mean

Custody does not by itself establish original copyright ownership over upstream Linux, GNU, or other third-party code.

## Draft — higher-assurance custody

**DRAFT:** Where a release requires a stronger legal or provenance guarantee, the project should preserve an evidence package sufficient for qualified review. A “Court Hold 4” designation is an internal project term unless an actual court order or other authoritative instrument establishes it externally. Likewise, an MIT license designation must be verified against the actual source and applicable license history.

Any contract, paid review, licensing fee, or other cost should be recorded only when an actual obligation or engagement exists; a hypothetical cost is not an incurred cost.

## Driver treatment

Kernel drivers originating upstream remain attributed to their original authors and licensors. A driver modified by MEARVK should retain its existing notices and receive a clear project modification/attention record where appropriate.

## Project statement

As of 2026, Max Rupplin / MEARVK LLC assumes project-level architectural custody and maintenance attention for the repository integration, subject to the licenses governing each component.